missing_token.description:
Home Assistant cannot start these bulbs and asks to power cycle them: {bulbs}.

That is usually the 49.7-day firmware lock. The guard can restart them from here, but it has no token for them. Add one in Settings → Devices & services → Yeelight Quota Guard → Configure.

Do you need to act? Yes.

{joke}
Burburito code: {code}

token_rejected.description:
{bulb} answers on the network but rejects the token the guard has. That happens when a bulb is reset or added again in the app. Fetch the tokens again from the integration's options.

Do you need to act? Yes, or this bulb will not be restarted.

{joke}
Burburito code: {code}

restart_failed.description:
{bulb} was asked to restart but did not come back within 90 seconds with a fresh uptime. Switch it off at the wall for ten seconds.

Do you need to act? Yes.

{joke}
Burburito code: {code}
